WEBVTT

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:19.330
Haru, what are you staring at?

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:22.910
The Miracle Jumbo Hope Lottery Ticket I got.

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:25.790
The winner's announced tomorrow.

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:28.880
You're not going to win.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:33.000
The odds are way worse than 
drawing ten five-stars in a row.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.120
That's right.

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:35.550
One of my aunts always buys these tickets.

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:41.060
Names like New Year's, Dream, 
Summer, Green, Autumn...

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:42.310
But she never wins.

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:44.990
But if we win, we get a trillion zel.

00:00:44.990 --> 00:00:46.590
I know, I know.

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:47.770
But you're not going to win.

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:51.530
Yeah, I guess you're right.

00:00:51.830 --> 00:00:55.670
But we'll know when we see tomorrow's paper,
 so I'll check anyway.

00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:56.940
Right, right.

00:00:56.940 --> 00:01:00.030
You're not going to win,
 so don't let it get you down.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.960
<b>Episode 4: Rich in Zel</b>

00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:34.340
Thanks.

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:35.400
You're welcome!

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:42.880
Let's see...

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:46.150
Whoa, what? You two are up already?

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:47.150
Just happened to be.

00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:50.050
I got up to use the bathroom, 
but thought I'd look.

00:02:50.050 --> 00:02:51.600
Let's look together.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:54.110
By the way, what's the number on the ticket?

00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:58.390
G-33965963.

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:00.950
G-33965963?

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:03.480
There's no way you'll win 
with a number that big.

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:04.800
Right...

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:06.620
Oh, here it is.

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:08.520
I know we didn't win.

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:11.130
Let's look so we can be done with this.

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:13.250
The winning number is...

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:16.580
G-33965963.

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:20.970
Told you.

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:22.720
You weren't going to win.

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:24.010
Yeah.

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:25.760
But it was close.

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:27.890
Really. It was so close.

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:29.860
We were so close.

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:34.160
But this one was G-33965963.

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:38.180
And this one is G-33965963.

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:46.970
It's so close. We almost got it...

00:03:46.970 --> 00:03:48.490
You won.

00:03:50.110 --> 00:03:51.960
We won!

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:03.480
Yes, this is a grand prize winning ticket.

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:05.180
Please come this way.

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:10.020
Before I give you your zel, there are
some things we have to go over.

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:14.700
It's better not to quit your job 
because you won a bunch of zel.

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:18.440
And it's better not to tell 
people that you've won...

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:20.030
We get it!

00:04:20.030 --> 00:04:21.000
Just open the vault!

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:22.480
Quick! Quick!

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:38.270
Amazing! We've got all this 
left after splitting it up!

00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:40.580
We're zellionaires now!

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:43.920
We won't have to eat plain curry 
for three days straight anymore!

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:45.840
We can eat steak every day!

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:47.680
I can eat chocolate every day.

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:50.750
You can make a house out of 
chocolate and live in it.

00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:52.600
Okay, I will!

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:54.120
That's right! A house!

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:57.320
I'm moving into a new house,
 buying furniture...

00:04:57.320 --> 00:05:02.320
Oh, and I'm buying back twice the amount
of clothes that got sold off the other day!

00:05:06.260 --> 00:05:10.320
The Jumbo Hope Lottery Ticket 
we got as a reward won!

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:13.750
Now we can rebuild the branch office!

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:19.600
No, this was our reward.

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:22.300
We don't need to give 
it to the branch office.

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:25.010
I think it's fine.

00:05:25.890 --> 00:05:28.080
We got more than we could ever use.

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:29.350
We could give them some.

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:32.390
I'm against it.

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:37.390
Then I'll give you enough 
to rebuild from my share.

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:38.770
Seriously?

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:41.240
You're such a softy.

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:43.060
Yay!

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:49.870
Did we go too far?

00:05:50.140 --> 00:05:53.800
You need something like this if you 
want to get rid of the nicknames

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:56.750
we got since our funds were stolen, 
like "The Poor Branch Office,"

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:58.960
"The Losers' Branch Office," 
"The Moron's Branch Office,"

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:02.920
and "The Embarrassing Branch Office."

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:05.590
Did people really call us 
"The Embarrassing Branch Office"?

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:07.840
Ahem.

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:12.830
Anyway, now we've got tons of 
periods who want to work for us.

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:13.970
What? Really?

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:19.390
I always wanted to work for this place.

00:06:19.390 --> 00:06:20.660
Me, too.

00:06:20.660 --> 00:06:23.280
I just happened to hear that they 
pay twice what everybody else does,

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:24.900
but that's not why.

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:27.920
I always wanted to work here.

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:31.770
They don't have quotas,
 but that doesn't matter, either.

00:06:31.770 --> 00:06:35.380
I always wanted to work here, too.

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:38.330
Good.

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:40.930
Now, Branch Office #8 is finally back.

00:06:40.930 --> 00:06:42.100
Yes.

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:44.700
I can never thank Haru enough.

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:49.640
Oh, by the way, they all built huge 
mansions on the west side of town.

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:51.720
Oh, really?

00:06:56.960 --> 00:06:58.640
Clean carefully.

00:06:58.880 --> 00:07:02.710
It's important to clean, clean, 
and then clean some more.

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:11.700
This is amazing!

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:13.810
Don't get too excited, Gajeru.

00:07:13.810 --> 00:07:14.530
It's indecent.

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:16.120
Gimme more.

00:07:16.550 --> 00:07:19.960
Is it okay to live this luxuriously?

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:24.160
Haru, the rich have a 
duty to spend their zel.

00:07:24.160 --> 00:07:27.550
If you hoard it, the economy can't function.

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:28.880
That's right!

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:31.440
Let's spend that cash and spin the economy!

00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:32.150
That's right!

00:07:32.150 --> 00:07:33.890
Spend and spin!

00:07:38.650 --> 00:07:41.810
Everybody, we got a quest 
to exterminate spirals!

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:42.890
Okay, it's here! I've been waiting!

00:07:42.890 --> 00:07:44.220
Let's go!

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:51.740
They're taking forever...

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:54.930
Here we are!

00:07:56.580 --> 00:07:58.450
What are those outfits?

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:00.310
It's this year's latest design!

00:08:00.310 --> 00:08:01.050
Does it look good?

00:08:01.050 --> 00:08:03.950
If you buy the whole set, you get this, too!

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:06.040
I couldn't wait to wear it!

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:08.260
Only ten of mine were ever made.

00:08:08.260 --> 00:08:10.360
It was hard to reserve one.

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:11.790
I see.

00:08:11.790 --> 00:08:13.300
Okay, let's go.

00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:14.650
Wait, Haru.

00:08:14.650 --> 00:08:15.540
What?

00:08:15.540 --> 00:08:17.140
Let's take this.

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:24.850
Welcome, welcome!

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:29.390
I'm the Mayor of Poor Village,
 Mayor Penniless.

00:08:29.390 --> 00:08:34.950
Spirals have settled in our potato fields, 
and now we're potato poor, too!

00:08:35.420 --> 00:08:37.280
Leave it to us!

00:08:40.010 --> 00:08:41.710
Look at them all...

00:08:41.710 --> 00:08:45.350
They just started multiplying 
out of nowhere,

00:08:45.350 --> 00:08:47.550
like my debts after I started gambling!

00:08:47.550 --> 00:08:51.060
Huh? They're all Level 1 spirals,

00:08:51.060 --> 00:08:53.120
but can we beat this many?

00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:56.630
If the three of us fight together, 
I think it'll work out, don't you?

00:08:56.630 --> 00:09:02.220
If we fight over there, we'll get 
mud on all our nice new clothes.

00:09:02.220 --> 00:09:04.180
Yeah, I guess so.

00:09:05.030 --> 00:09:07.780
Listen, I was thinking.

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:09.730
How badly do you really need potatoes?

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:10.980
What?

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:12.790
That's right.

00:09:12.790 --> 00:09:15.950
If they have no potatoes, 
let them eat melons!

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:17.060
That's right.

00:09:17.060 --> 00:09:18.520
Melons are sweeter.

00:09:18.520 --> 00:09:19.700
Hey, you two!

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:20.790
It was a joke.

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:22.820
Yeah, just a joke.

00:09:23.670 --> 00:09:25.620
Okay, let's do this...

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:27.590
Hold it!

00:09:27.590 --> 00:09:28.170
Who's there?

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:31.380
Come on, you know who that is by now.

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:32.800
I'm used to it at this point.

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:36.360
Hey, don't talk like you're 
tired of us already.

00:09:36.360 --> 00:09:37.540
It's rude, guru.

00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:39.460
Not doing your big entrance this week?

00:09:39.460 --> 00:09:40.390
Oh, right.

00:09:44.240 --> 00:09:44.850
Mizaru.

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:49.190
Kikazaru!

00:09:51.830 --> 00:09:53.530
Iwazaru and Guru!

00:09:53.530 --> 00:09:55.110
Together, we are...

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:55.590
Wi!

00:09:55.590 --> 00:09:55.900
Se!

00:09:55.900 --> 00:09:56.610
Man!

00:09:58.280 --> 00:09:59.410
Wiseman!

00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:02.810
Too bad for you, guys!

00:10:02.810 --> 00:10:06.200
We, Wiseman, will be stealing this quest!

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:08.220
This is our quest.

00:10:08.220 --> 00:10:09.420
We won't let you have it!

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:11.560
Oh, sure. Go for it.

00:10:11.560 --> 00:10:12.310
What?

00:10:12.310 --> 00:10:16.910
That's right. I was just wishing 
I didn't have to do it.

00:10:16.910 --> 00:10:19.010
We'll throw in some extra zel if you take it.

00:10:19.010 --> 00:10:20.240
Seriously?!

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:21.360
I just noticed this,

00:10:21.360 --> 00:10:23.380
but aren't your outfits a 
little fancier than usual?

00:10:23.380 --> 00:10:25.520
Well, maybe.

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:27.210
So, how about it?

00:10:27.210 --> 00:10:29.680
Up for some subcontracting, kiddos?

00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:32.300
Wow, they're already talking 
like they're better than us.

00:10:32.300 --> 00:10:33.940
I don't like the way they talk.

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:35.280
It makes me sick.

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:36.440
Yeah, yeah!

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:38.450
We'll double your zel.

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:39.910
We're in!

00:11:02.660 --> 00:11:04.050
What are you doing here?

00:11:04.050 --> 00:11:07.020
I just don't like sitting on the sidelines.

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:09.240
You really are a softy.

00:11:09.240 --> 00:11:11.930
You can help, but you can't 
have any of the money.

00:11:11.930 --> 00:11:12.850
Yeah, yeah!

00:11:22.940 --> 00:11:26.740
Thank you! Here's your humble reward!

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:28.420
You saved us!

00:11:28.420 --> 00:11:29.620
Thank you!

00:11:31.850 --> 00:11:33.890
Thanks. You were a big help.

00:11:33.890 --> 00:11:37.780
I hope you'll keep showing up.

00:11:37.780 --> 00:11:39.760
There's more subcontracting for you.

00:11:41.280 --> 00:11:43.260
I don't like those guys...

00:11:43.260 --> 00:11:46.040
If I ever become a zellionaire, 
I don't want to be like that.

00:11:46.040 --> 00:11:47.390
Yeah, yeah!

00:11:51.090 --> 00:11:52.770
You're covered in mud!

00:11:53.050 --> 00:11:54.640
We're paying them zel.

00:11:54.640 --> 00:11:56.950
Why did you help?

00:12:07.220 --> 00:12:08.990
This isn't right!

00:12:08.990 --> 00:12:09.900
What isn't?

00:12:09.900 --> 00:12:14.520
I think it's wrong to let someone else 
do a job you took because you're rich.

00:12:14.520 --> 00:12:16.130
Why?

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:18.550
They were happy to have the job.

00:12:18.550 --> 00:12:20.900
But solving problems with zel is...

00:12:21.460 --> 00:12:22.730
So what?

00:12:22.730 --> 00:12:24.950
Should we have picked a 
fight with them instead?

00:12:24.950 --> 00:12:27.780
No, but this doesn't feel right.

00:12:27.780 --> 00:12:31.220
I don't understand why you can have zel,
 but not be allowed to use it.

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:33.440
But...

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:35.610
Fine.

00:12:35.610 --> 00:12:37.370
So we'll split up the party, then.

00:12:37.830 --> 00:12:41.400
There's no need to be in a party with 
people who have different values.

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:42.950
That's right.

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:44.510
I've got plenty of zel,

00:12:44.510 --> 00:12:46.360
so I'm going to take a
 break from being a period.

00:12:46.840 --> 00:12:48.270
So let's split up.

00:12:48.270 --> 00:12:48.910
Bye!

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:51.250
Wait!

00:12:53.370 --> 00:12:56.440
Want to hit up Bar Saka in Dail?

00:12:56.440 --> 00:12:58.160
Where's that?

00:13:01.960 --> 00:13:03.970
<b>~ the journey to the end of the despair ~</b>

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:10.140
This is good stuff.

00:13:10.480 --> 00:13:11.400
Thanks, boss.

00:13:11.400 --> 00:13:14.610
Blood Realm merchandise is always good.

00:13:14.610 --> 00:13:16.920
Okay, buy out the whole factory.

00:13:16.920 --> 00:13:19.400
Buy out any finished products, too.

00:13:19.400 --> 00:13:20.200
Yes, sir.

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:23.600
What else we got?

00:13:23.600 --> 00:13:25.610
In a blood realm used bookstore, a Sapphire—

00:13:25.960 --> 00:13:27.930
Call her Sapphire-sama, damn it!

00:13:27.930 --> 00:13:28.940
I'm sorry, sir!

00:13:28.940 --> 00:13:33.080
A complete collection of Sapphire-sama 
photo albums was found,

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:35.000
and in mint condition!

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:38.090
Just buy out the store, obviously!

00:13:38.090 --> 00:13:42.250
Buy all Sapphire-san merchandise as 
soon as you find it, new or used.

00:13:42.250 --> 00:13:42.590
Yes, sir!

00:13:42.920 --> 00:13:44.800
There's no limit to how much zel I'll spend!

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:50.090
I'll raise Sapphire-san into a bigger 
superstar than she already is!

00:13:55.310 --> 00:13:57.760
This is quite nice.

00:13:57.760 --> 00:13:59.930
It's from the Sky Realm.

00:13:59.930 --> 00:14:02.620
It was made in the country of angels?

00:14:02.620 --> 00:14:03.690
Indeed.

00:14:03.690 --> 00:14:06.870
If it's from the Sky Realm, it must be good.

00:14:06.870 --> 00:14:09.480
A crystal ball of ultimate good luck.

00:14:09.480 --> 00:14:10.660
I'll buy it.

00:14:10.960 --> 00:14:12.540
Thank you.

00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:17.120
This is a Good Luck Grimoire 
from the Blood Realm.

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:18.760
Of course, I'll take it.

00:14:18.760 --> 00:14:22.050
A good luck amplifier from the Hell Realm.

00:14:22.050 --> 00:14:23.230
I'll take it.

00:14:23.230 --> 00:14:26.160
A monkey's paw from the Animal Realm.

00:14:26.160 --> 00:14:27.290
I'll take it.

00:14:27.290 --> 00:14:28.760
A picture of dolphins.

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:29.660
I'll take it.

00:14:29.660 --> 00:14:31.160
Sakurada's pot.

00:14:31.160 --> 00:14:32.000
I'll take it!

00:14:32.000 --> 00:14:33.430
A water purifier!

00:14:33.430 --> 00:14:34.980
This is taking too long!

00:14:34.980 --> 00:14:36.540
I'll take it all!

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:38.710
Just leave it all here!

00:14:52.670 --> 00:14:54.340
Watch out!

00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:58.920
That was close, huh?

00:14:58.920 --> 00:15:02.300
Now, we saved you, so you have to thank us.

00:15:02.300 --> 00:15:04.820
Wait, you're the one who 
always got in our way.

00:15:04.820 --> 00:15:05.790
It's Haruharu!

00:15:05.790 --> 00:15:06.820
Haruharu?

00:15:06.820 --> 00:15:09.880
No, you're the ones who 
always got in our way.

00:15:09.880 --> 00:15:12.210
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:15:12.210 --> 00:15:14.720
Anyway, why are you alone?

00:15:15.870 --> 00:15:18.430
Well, the party split up.

00:15:18.430 --> 00:15:20.190
Now, I'm alone.

00:15:20.190 --> 00:15:22.430
Isn't that dangerous?

00:15:22.430 --> 00:15:25.560
But I heard you're a zellionaire, too.

00:15:25.560 --> 00:15:28.400
You could just go off and be 
rich instead of doing this.

00:15:28.770 --> 00:15:32.680
I just get nervous if 
I'm not doing something.

00:15:34.210 --> 00:15:36.870
He's just a commoner at heart.

00:15:37.270 --> 00:15:38.700
Well, fine.

00:15:38.700 --> 00:15:41.740
Anyway, we saved you, so now you owe us.

00:15:42.360 --> 00:15:44.080
You can come be our servant for a while.

00:15:47.640 --> 00:15:48.620
Servant!

00:15:48.620 --> 00:15:49.440
Yes?

00:15:49.440 --> 00:15:50.880
Go buy me some yakisoba bread.

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:51.810
Okay!

00:15:51.810 --> 00:15:53.280
I want some melon bread!

00:15:54.800 --> 00:15:55.900
She says she wants curry bread.

00:15:55.900 --> 00:15:56.660
Bean jam bread, guru.

00:15:56.660 --> 00:15:57.570
Chocolate croissant.

00:15:57.570 --> 00:15:59.890
Okay!

00:16:02.660 --> 00:16:06.200
Nobody was selling them, so I had to 
go all the way to the next village.

00:16:06.200 --> 00:16:09.360
It's as if there are five Chocos.

00:16:14.680 --> 00:16:16.990
Mister, let me give you some advice.

00:16:16.990 --> 00:16:19.280
Give us all you've got and disappear!

00:16:19.280 --> 00:16:21.080
Are you bandits?

00:16:21.520 --> 00:16:24.960
Hey, do you think you can beat us alone?

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:28.250
Don't touch him.

00:16:29.180 --> 00:16:31.320
I wondered why you were late!

00:16:36.430 --> 00:16:39.140
We'll get you for this!

00:16:39.450 --> 00:16:40.750
Thank you, everyone!

00:16:40.750 --> 00:16:44.280
It's a boss's job to take 
care of her idiot servant.

00:16:44.280 --> 00:16:45.890
It's fine.

00:16:45.890 --> 00:16:47.730
Haru's just an idiot.

00:16:47.730 --> 00:16:50.110
Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow, ow!

00:16:58.200 --> 00:16:59.050
Liza!

00:16:59.050 --> 00:16:59.700
Gajeru!

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:04.040
What's with that outfit? You look so dumb.

00:17:04.040 --> 00:17:04.720
What?

00:17:04.720 --> 00:17:07.860
You look like you tried to be 
a godfather and screwed up bad!

00:17:18.840 --> 00:17:19.930
What?!

00:17:19.930 --> 00:17:22.610
Oh, hello, Gajeru-san.

00:17:22.610 --> 00:17:24.510
There was an ugly building here,

00:17:24.510 --> 00:17:29.480
so I decided to put up a prettier one to 
show how architecture should be.

00:17:29.480 --> 00:17:32.560
I didn't realize it was yours, though.

00:17:32.560 --> 00:17:34.540
What?

00:17:37.990 --> 00:17:39.400
What? What? What?

00:17:42.460 --> 00:17:44.200
Sorry, sorry.

00:17:44.200 --> 00:17:47.050
I thought you were a pebble, 
so I didn't notice you.

00:17:47.050 --> 00:17:53.360
Still, hard to believe somebody as rich as 
you is riding around on that tiny thing!

00:17:54.270 --> 00:17:55.800
What?!

00:18:05.360 --> 00:18:06.230
What?

00:18:06.230 --> 00:18:08.280
Oh, excuse me.

00:18:08.280 --> 00:18:11.100
I thought you were a floating leaf,
 so I didn't notice you.

00:18:11.100 --> 00:18:17.310
Still, hard to believe somebody as rich 
as you is riding around on that tiny boat!

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:21.620
<b>Liza</b>

00:18:45.270 --> 00:18:47.080
What is this?

00:18:47.080 --> 00:18:49.430
Sculptures I donated to the city.

00:18:49.430 --> 00:18:51.790
It should boost tourism.

00:18:55.520 --> 00:18:56.600
Don't tell me...

00:18:56.600 --> 00:18:59.440
Sculptures I donated to the city.

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:17.840
Mine are going to get there first!

00:19:17.840 --> 00:19:20.800
No, mine are going to get there first!

00:19:35.770 --> 00:19:37.860
You've got guts, Liza.

00:19:38.480 --> 00:19:41.450
Yeah, so do you.

00:19:42.470 --> 00:19:44.400
I guess we should stop hating each other.

00:19:44.400 --> 00:19:45.380
Yeah.

00:19:45.380 --> 00:19:48.340
We should both put our 
zel toward better uses.

00:19:50.540 --> 00:19:52.540
Liza-sama!

00:19:53.120 --> 00:19:54.100
Liza-sama!

00:19:54.100 --> 00:19:57.940
The servants betrayed us and 
ran off with all the money!

00:19:59.060 --> 00:20:02.130
Gajeru-sama's servants did the same thing!

00:20:02.560 --> 00:20:04.850
This has nothing to do with that,

00:20:04.850 --> 00:20:08.320
but everything Branch Office #8
 owns was stolen again!

00:20:20.280 --> 00:20:21.650
Plain curry, huh?

00:20:22.520 --> 00:20:25.050
We're totally back to where we started.

00:20:25.050 --> 00:20:26.800
Oh, well.

00:20:26.800 --> 00:20:29.030
I guess the three of us start over.

00:20:29.030 --> 00:20:30.120
That's just how it goes.

00:20:31.080 --> 00:20:32.610
Um, well...

00:20:32.610 --> 00:20:33.480
What?

00:20:33.480 --> 00:20:34.690
What's up, Haru?

00:20:34.690 --> 00:20:37.630
I'm Wiseman's servant now...

00:20:38.470 --> 00:20:40.630
Oh, they fired you.

00:20:40.630 --> 00:20:43.400
Mizaru said you were useless.

00:20:43.400 --> 00:20:45.980
Was I that bad?

00:20:45.980 --> 00:20:47.960
I don't get it, but...

00:20:47.960 --> 00:20:49.980
That means we can party together again?

00:20:50.830 --> 00:20:52.280
Yeah, that's right.

00:20:52.280 --> 00:20:54.280
Okay, glad to be back with you guys!

00:20:54.280 --> 00:20:55.460
Yeah!

00:21:00.420 --> 00:21:02.090
Good luck, servant.

00:21:02.090 --> 00:21:04.510
Haruharu was handy to have around.

00:21:18.550 --> 00:21:21.820
My hands used to be covered in gems,
but now they're covered in mud.

00:21:21.820 --> 00:21:22.950
Don't say that.

00:21:22.950 --> 00:21:24.320
It just makes me sad.

00:21:24.320 --> 00:21:27.050
But I'm happy the three of 
us are back together again.

00:21:27.720 --> 00:21:30.400
We can make zel by fighting lots of spirals.

00:21:30.400 --> 00:21:33.450
We're back to doing
 unlicensed jobs, so we can't.

00:21:33.450 --> 00:21:38.260
Hey, what happened to the zel you had that 
you didn't give to the Branch Office, Haru?

00:21:39.040 --> 00:21:40.270
I'm saving it all.

00:21:41.870 --> 00:21:43.740
Hey, lend me just a little.

00:21:43.740 --> 00:21:44.240
Me, too!

00:21:44.240 --> 00:21:45.240
I can't do that.

00:21:45.240 --> 00:21:48.080
All Haru's zel is going to buy me snacks.

00:21:48.080 --> 00:21:49.950
How much are you planning on eating?

00:21:50.760 --> 00:21:53.160
I'll eat endlessly, like I'm breathing.

00:21:53.160 --> 00:21:54.490
Please, lend me some!

00:21:54.490 --> 00:21:56.900
No, you'll just waste it!

00:21:56.900 --> 00:21:57.980
I won't!

00:21:57.980 --> 00:21:59.160
I promise!

00:21:59.160 --> 00:22:01.110
I don't want the party splitting up.

00:22:01.110 --> 00:22:02.420
It won'! It won't!

00:22:02.420 --> 00:22:03.980
I promise!

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.930
<b>Episode 5
"The Swamp's Name"</b>

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.930
<b>Preview</b>

00:23:36.740 --> 00:23:38.420
The Swamp's Name.
